{
  "id": "Compound::DB01283 - Gene::1559",
  "verbalization": "Lumiracoxib, a selective COX-2 inhibitor, is shown to bind to Cyp2c19, a cytochrome P450 enzyme involved in the metabolism of various substrates. This binding is consistent across multiple paths, with all three evidence streams reporting that Cyp2c19 participates in the same type of monooxygenase activity—specifically, the oxidation of limonene. The shared participation in this activity by Cyp2c9 suggests a potential functional link between Lumiracoxib and Cyp2c9, as the enzyme is a known participant in the metabolic pathway of limonene. The high scores from the three paths indicate a strong, consistent relationship, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence supports a mechanistic pathway where Lumiracoxib may modulate the activity of Cyp2c9 through its interaction with Cyp2c19, potentially affecting the metabolism of limonene and other substrates.",
